### Tier 4 marketplace demo — modular monolith + multi-tenancy + RS256 JWT
### Open in VS Code with REST Client and run requests top-to-bottom.
### The first four requests mint role-specific tokens via the Development-only
### /demo/token issuer. Subsequent requests present the JWT as
### `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`, flowing through ASP.NET Core's
### UseAuthentication / UseAuthorization / role policies / tenant filter.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@tenant = acme
@globexTenant = globex
@sellerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@buyerId  = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@otherBuyerId = 44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444
@adminId  = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### --- OIDC discovery (always available; publishes the public key) ---
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

###
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### --- Mint demo tokens (Development-only issuer; RS256) ---

# @name sellerToken
GET {{host}}/demo/token?role=Seller&tenant={{tenant}}&userId={{sellerId}}

# @name buyerToken
GET {{host}}/demo/token?role=Buyer&tenant={{tenant}}&userId={{buyerId}}

# @name otherBuyerToken
GET {{host}}/demo/token?role=Buyer&tenant={{tenant}}&userId={{otherBuyerId}}

# @name adminToken
GET {{host}}/demo/token?role=Admin&tenant={{tenant}}&userId={{adminId}}

# @name globexBuyerToken
GET {{host}}/demo/token?role=Buyer&tenant={{globexTenant}}&userId={{buyerId}}

### --- Fetch published products (Acme tenant) ---
# @name listed
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Globex buyer sees only Globex catalog (multi-tenancy demo)
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
Authorization: Bearer {{globexBuyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### S1: Seller creates a product
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sample Widget", "price": 15.00, "stock": 25 }

### S2: Empty name -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "price": 10.00, "stock": 5 }

### S3: Zero price -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
Authorization: Bearer {{sellerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Free", "price": 0, "stock": 5 }

### S4: Buyer places order (sufficient stock, Widget) -> 201 Pending; saga confirms async
# @name placeOrder
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-place-widget-001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{listed.response.body.$[2].id}}", "quantity": 2 }

### Wait ~1s then fetch the order — status should be Confirmed
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### S5: Insufficient stock (Doohickey stock=0) -> 201 Pending; saga marks Failed
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{listed.response.body.$[0].id}}", "quantity": 1 }

### S7: Cancel own order
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Place another order for S8 / S9
# @name secondOrder
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{listed.response.body.$[1].id}}", "quantity": 1 }

### S8: Other buyer cancels -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/buyer/orders/{{secondOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{otherBuyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### S9: Admin force-cancels
POST {{host}}/api/admin/orders/{{secondOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### S10: Buyer list (suspended hidden)
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### S11: Admin list includes everything
GET {{host}}/api/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### S12: No Authorization header -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products

### S13: Wrong role -> 403 (Buyer token at a Seller endpoint)
POST {{host}}/api/seller/products
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Naughty", "price": 1.00, "stock": 1 }

### --- Feature flags demo (Acme tenant) ---

### List flags
GET {{host}}/api/admin/feature-flags
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Set EnablePremiumBadge rollout to 100%
PUT {{host}}/api/admin/feature-flags/EnablePremiumBadge/rollout
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "percentage": 100 }

### After cache TTL (~30s), buyer list shows isPremium: true
GET {{host}}/api/buyer/products
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
